,title,link,text,language,family
0,Music of Papua New Guinea - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Papua_New_Guinea,"December 18, 2025 - 1949 saw the first Papuan to achieve international fame, Blasius To Una, begin his career. By the end of the 1970s, a local recording industry had appeared and artists such as Sanguma and later George Telek began mixing native and Western styles like rock and jazz.",Waioli,West Papuan
1,Music - Free West Papua Campaign,https://www.freewestpapua.org/resources/music/,"April 2, 2026 - There have been a number of albums released in recent years in support of the Free West Papua movement. These span from music recorded by West Papuans (including Mambesak and the Lani Singers), through to compilation releases featuring artists supportive of the cause.",Waioli,West Papuan
2,"Papuan Strings, Pt. 3: Wisisi — aural archipelago",https://www.auralarchipelago.com/auralarchipelago/wisisi,"May 7, 2024 - There are only a handful of picking patterns (“Wisisi/Iniki One” is the main one which provides the music it’s name, but there’s also “Nakwewa,” “Wiranare,” and “Shogiara”), but the verses are endless, and each village, each region has its own. Life is changing rapidly in the Papuan highlands, and though not yet half a century in the making, these honai-spun acoustic wisisi tunes are already being seen as “old school.” “Nobody down here [in the city] knows the old songs, the real iniki one” Pak Jami lamented as I asked him about his youth picking out tunes at courtship rituals.",Waioli,West Papuan
3,West Papua Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLnOSH5j1sQh_2l75fHfbp91Lu72FYJqHI,A war of independence has waged in West Papua for some time. The people are Melanesian. Indonesian influence is felt in West Papuan music.,Waioli,West Papuan
4,Etai Wisisi Waga O Wamena Hanorasuok - YES NO WAVE MUSIC,https://yesnowave.bandcamp.com/album/etai-wisisi-waga-o-wamena-hanorasuok,"Drag him to any dance floor in the highlands of West Papua, though, and the kid turns into a star. Except it won’t look like your garden variety dance gig. The music is fast paced, relentless, almost trance-inducing.",Waioli,West Papuan
5,‘Music Helps a West Papuan Feeling’: Transporting Selves and ...,https://sebsalay.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/bfe_music-helps-a-west-papuan-feeling-transporting-selves-and-moving-others_salay.pdf,"In this paper I show how music transports West Papuan musicians, how they then use music to move their audiences, and how this supports the broader political movement. I also consider forms of immobility that contextualise these movements.",Waioli,West Papuan
6,"West Papua Music Collection | Reggae from nabire, ID",https://www.reverbnation.com/westpapuamusiccollection,"Reggae music, lyrics, and videos from nabire, ID on ReverbNation",Waioli,West Papuan
7,The Spirit of Mambesak West Papuan Freedom Music - The Commons,https://commonslibrary.org/the-spirit-of-mambesak-west-papuan-freedom-music/,"February 15, 2026 - Other Papuan pop bands have recorded patriotic songs that challenged the Indonesian control of a country that for decades they referred to as Irian Jaya – Trio Ambisi’s Tanah Papua being another example, or Edo Konodologit’s Aku Papua. In the late 80’s, an art-rock band from Melbourne called Not Drowning, Waving arrived in Papua New Guinea. They were interested initially in the music of the country, but while there they encountered West Papuan refugees fleeing violence and living in the Blackwater refugee camp near the border.",Waioli,West Papuan
